// Figures fact-checked in October 2026 against the sources listed with each entry.
//
// Each entry is one variant of an item (e.g. item 'Beef': steak, burger). The first
// entry of an item is its default, used when comparing against it.
// Each entry gives either:
//   g:   [low, central, high] grams CO2e per unit, and/or
//   kwh: [low, central, high] kWh per unit; grams = g + kWh × grid intensity.
// [low, high] is least to most possible (the Range view). Where an entry has both g and kwh, each
// position is one scenario (e.g. small car: little fuel, more electricity), so kwh alone need not be in order.
// low == high means only one sourced figure exists, so no range is shown.
// Entries with km: give g or kwh per passenger-km, and km is the length of an average
// one-way trip, the default distance. Entries with amt and unit give figures for amt of
// unit (e.g. 200 g), the default amount; others count units. avg describes the default
// amount, e.g. 'average'.
// Figures are world averages. unc: how far off the average may be, in % (10: physics or measured;
// 25: three or more world sources agree, or the maker's report for that exact model; 50: within 1.5×;
// 100: within 2× or one source; 200: worse). Items at 100 or more are shown faded and left out of comparisons.
// region: a country's own figure, listed only when that country's grid is chosen.
// calc: [factor, amount, what] terms; the central figure is the sum of amount × FACTORS[factor].g
// (g[1] is then null). checks: [title, url, grams] whole-item estimates by others, to compare against.

